title: 'Schemas: where a framework for it already exists, a new association is learned in one trial and consolidated in two days; without one, it is not.'
pid: 57a98ada-4e8c-4793-bac3-1378f921380d
body: |2-
  Tse and others, Science, 2007, in rats learning which flavour lies
  where. Top found the same in tending, from three cases: a reader of
  a plan files its reading well if its graph already has the place
  for it, and on top if it has none, so a newborn's first graph is the
  one to expect to move (in "what a specialist is", in the team note).
